  - Choose appropriate visibility modifiers for classes, methods, and attributes.
  - Comments should be appropriate in amount and consistently written either in English or German.
  - Comply with all Checkstyle rules; certain marked Checkstyle violations cause an automatic zero.
  - Do not add personal data other than your u‑Kürzel to submissions.
  - Do not use the default package for your classes.
  - Error messages must not contain special characters such as newlines or umlauts.
  - Every error message must begin with the exact prefix "Error:" with no leading spaces.
  - Follow all whitespace rules enforced by the Checkstyle configuration.
  - Follow Javadoc documentation rules and include only the u‑Kürzel in the Javadoc author tag.
  - If user input does not match the expected format or a command cannot be executed, print an error
   message.
  - Maximum line width of source files is 120 characters.
  - Never reassign the standard streams (System.in, System.out, System.err).
  - Only java.util.Scanner and elements from the listed packages may be used from the Java library
